{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:19:57.681150663Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-53334dc5","body":"In `PROVENANCE_STATUS.md`, the denitrification parameters section (lines 46-61) contains a TODO note: \"Extend `ProcessParamsPreset` to include denitrification fields, then attach formal `param_meta` entries.\" This TODO references tanksim-6e5.7.2 in `default.toml` (line 206-207: `TODO(tanksim-6e5.7.2): extend ProcessParamsPreset to carry denitrification fields so param_meta can be attached`). Since this bead IS 6e5.7.2, the TODO should either be resolved within this bead or the tag should be updated to reference a future bead (e.g., a new dedicated bead or G3/G4). Leaving a self-referencing TODO creates confusion about whether the work was intentionally deferred or accidentally omitted.","dedup_key":"27f746c9702bf53fa216746558c667d18a41748e0a6f7fc2297f7f2c850581eb","run_id":"run-20260330104128","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":15,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:19:57.690087046Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-5867a315","body":"The `tan_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l` and `no2_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l` default changes (2.0→3.0 and 1.0→1.5) are a behavioral correction, not just a metadata annotation. The shrimp TOML preset (`neocaridina_davidi.toml`) is updated to match, but there is no `param_meta` entry for `tan_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l` or `no2_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l` in the shrimp TOML despite these being newly corrected values with an explicit derivation rationale (preserving the legacy decline span). Adding `param_meta` for these two parameters would be consistent with the bead's goal and would capture the 'derived from legacy formula' provenance before it's lost.","dedup_key":"c3293b45ddf4af503ce2ea8fd687177c76fbee86094dafa28262a7035abfb8ce","run_id":"run-20260330104128","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
